## 11. Gold Coin Reward System

Implement a persistent in-game currency system.

### Reward Rules

Players receive gold coins after successfully completing a level.

Rewards should depend on:

* Level difficulty.
* Parking accuracy.
* Completion time.
* Collision count.
* Remaining vehicle condition.
* Successful completion of optional objectives.

Example reward structure:

| Performance                |              Reward |
| -------------------------- | ------------------: |
| Basic completion           |           100 coins |
| Good parking accuracy      |           150 coins |
| Excellent parking accuracy |           200 coins |
| Perfect parking            |           250 coins |
| Optional challenge bonus   | 50 additional coins |

These values are initial balancing suggestions and should be configurable.

Prevent duplicate rewards from being granted repeatedly for the same completion record. Players may earn coins again when replaying a level, but replay rewards must follow the defined reward rules.

### Currency Interface

Display:

* Current coin balance.
* Coins earned after each level.
* Coins required for vehicle purchases.
* Coins required for upgrades.
* Transaction feedback.

Save the coin balance so that it persists after the game is closed.

